---
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Artificial Intelligence — Conscia Labs"
  description="We study how AI agents use tools, work together, and operate within an organization’s security rules."
  noIndex
>
  <div class="focus-detail-shell">
    <Header />
    <section class="focus-detail-hero" aria-labelledby="focus-detail-title">
      <div class="container">
        <a class="back-link" href="/#focus-areas"><Arrow /> All focus areas</a>
        <div class="focus-detail-hero__grid">
          <div class="focus-detail-hero__copy">
            <p class="project-detail-meta">01 <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Focus area</p>
            <h1 id="focus-detail-title">Artificial Intelligence</h1>
            <p class="focus-detail-hero__lede">Agents that can act, without losing track of who’s in charge.</p>
            <p class="focus-detail-hero__description">We look at how AI agents plan and use tools. That includes how they work together over longer tasks. The hard part is giving them enough freedom to help, without losing control of what they can do.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="agentic-map" aria-label="A conceptual map of an agentic system">
            <div class="agentic-map__orbit agentic-map__orbit--outer"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__orbit agentic-map__orbit--inner"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--one"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--two"></div>
            <div class="agentic-map__connection agentic-map__connection--three"></div>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--agent">AGENT</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--protocol">A2A</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--security">SECURITY</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__node agentic-map__node--context">CONTEXT</span>
            <span class="agentic-map__boundary">ENTERPRISE BOUNDARY</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-overview section-light" aria-labelledby="focus-question-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">01 / The challenge</p>
          <h2 id="focus-question-title">Agents need limits.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-overview__copy">
          <p>An agent can plan a task and call tools. It might also hand a step to another system. That raises some basic questions: whose permissions is it using, what data can it see, and who’s responsible for the result?</p>
          <p>We work on patterns an organization can use: limits on what an agent can do, and a record of what it did.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-threads section-dark" aria-labelledby="threads-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--dark">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">02 / Current threads</p>
            <h2 id="threads-title">What we’re looking into.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The agent is only one part of the picture. We also study how systems communicate and how access is controlled.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-thread-grid">
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-bright)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">01</span>
            <h3>Agentic systems</h3>
            <p>Can an agent keep track of a long task? We test planning, tool use, coordination, and recovery when something goes wrong.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-info)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">02</span>
            <h3>Protocols and coordination</h3>
            <p>We study A2A and initiatives such as Agntcy. How do agents find each other, pass along a task, and make responsibility clear?</p>
          </article>
          <article class="focus-detail-thread" style="--item-accent: var(--accent-secondary)">
            <span class="focus-detail-thread__number">03</span>
            <h3>Enterprise security</h3>
            <p>We look at whose identity an agent uses and what it’s allowed to access. Permissions, policies, and audit records need to hold up when an agent calls a tool.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-boundaries section-light" aria-labelledby="boundaries-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">03 / Guardrails</p>
            <h2 id="boundaries-title">Be clear about an agent’s job.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>An agent needs room to help, with clear limits on what it can and can’t do.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-grid">
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">DEFINE</span>
            <h3>Who is it acting for?</h3>
            <p>Connect the agent to a person, team, service, or approved workflow. Its permissions should have a clear owner.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">OBSERVE</span>
            <h3>Keep a record.</h3>
            <p>Record decisions, tool calls, handoffs, and results so someone can review what happened.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="boundary-card">
            <span class="boundary-card__marker">CONTAIN</span>
            <h3>Decide where it has to stop.</h3>
            <p>Set limits on data, tools, and the task itself. Decide when the agent should stop or ask for help if conditions change.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-practice section-dark" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-practice__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">04 / How we work</p>
          <h2 id="practice-title">Put the ideas to the test.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="focus-detail-practice__steps">
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>01</span>
            <p><strong>Study</strong> what agents can do, how they communicate, and where they fail.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>02</span>
            <p><strong>Test</strong> the ideas against security rules and day-to-day operations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-step">
            <span>03</span>
            <p><strong>Build</strong> prototypes, guidance, and products people can try.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="focus-detail-cta section-dark" aria-labelledby="ai-cta-title">
      <div class="container focus-detail-cta__inner">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">Related project</p>
          <h2 id="ai-cta-title">Model access through AI Gateway.</h2>
          <p>AI Gateway manages model access for organizations, with access controls and separate tenants. It’s currently in closed beta.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button--outline" href="/projects/ai-gateway">Explore AI Gateway <Arrow /></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>
